    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0540" n="458" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1459.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-04-17"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 472.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    telegraphic instructions of April 14 and April 17,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d655-f1"
                    /> regarding the serious consequences that may flow from a repetition of such
                    incidents as those taking place during the fighting at Agua Prieta on the 13th
                    instant, I have the honor to inclose to the Department herewith copy of a note
                    which I addressed to the foreign office immediately upon receipt of the
                    Department’s first telegram. * * *</p>
                <p>I have [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d655-a1.xml" xpointer="d655-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
